## Copy to local.properties and fill in your SDK path
sdk.dir=/Users/YourName/Library/Android/sdk

## OAuth client IDs for the cloud-sync providers (optional).
##
## Each self-hosted install registers its own OAuth clients — there are no shared
## ones to ship. Leave a key out and that provider stays unconfigured; the app
## treats an empty id as "not set up" rather than sending a request the provider
## can only reject. The same values can be passed as environment variables of the
## same name instead, which take precedence (that is what CI uses).
##
## Register at:
##   Google     https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials  (OAuth client, type "Android")
##   Microsoft  https://entra.microsoft.com  → App registrations
##   Dropbox    https://www.dropbox.com/developers/apps
##
## The redirect URI to register in all three is: nagellacke://oauth
# OAUTH_CLIENT_ID_GOOGLE=xxxxxxxx.apps.googleusercontent.com
# OAUTH_CLIENT_ID_MICROSOFT=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
# OAUTH_CLIENT_ID_DROPBOX=xxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
